## Conventions

_Anything an engineer joining today would get wrong. Patterns in use, naming, structure,
what is deliberately not done here._

**An assertion is proven by breaking what it guards and watching it fail.** One nobody has broken
is decoration, and a gate that passes reads the same as a gate that had nothing to check.
`./.os/verify-mutation.sh --file <path> --delete-line '<pattern>' --gate '<command>'` is that break
as a command: it applies the mutation, runs the gates, restores the file, and fails unless a gate
failed. Exit 3 means the mutation matched nothing, so the run proved nothing.

